# Deploy the public site only. Everything at the repository root is excluded
# and the public pages are re-included explicitly, so working files, source
# projects, previews and media cannot become public routes by accident.
/*

!assets/
# HELD Readings are not published: their cards live in docs/held-readings.html,
# outside the deploy, and their images stay out of it too.
assets/reading-patagonia.webp
assets/reading-muji.webp
assets/reading-wd40.webp
assets/reading-new-yorker.webp
# The nail-bench photograph is retired from OFFER and not served.
assets/kill-dull-nailbench.webp
!api/

# ASK KILL DULL asks the model nothing while the free-text field is out, so
# the endpoint it would call is not built. Both files stay in the repository,
# reviewed and ready; deleting these two lines and restoring the maxDuration
# entry in vercel.json puts the endpoint back.
api/ask.js
api/_lib/
# The collection modules the functions import. Tests live in test/, which
# is deliberately NOT re-included: anything under a deployed directory is
# served as a file, and test sources are not public documents.
!lib/
!vercel.json
!robots.txt
!favicon.ico
!sitemap.xml
!404.html

!index.html
!why.html
!how.html
!offer.html
!outcome.html
!bureau.html
!accessibility.html
!privacy.html
!terms.html
!contact.html
!assessment.html
